[15d9820929ebad5b] KmsMain: Contract bug found, needs a header decision (affects every slice that calls to_exynos7580()):

`struct exynos7580_device` embeds `struct drm_device drm` and `to_exynos7580()` is container_of(). But 3.10 `drm_platform_init()` -> `drm_get_platform_dev()` does `dev = kzalloc(sizeof(struct drm_device))` itself (drivers/gpu/drm/drm_platform.c:42-60 in K3.10) — the drm_device is NOT inside our allocation, so container_of() returns garbage at runtime. There is no drm_dev_alloc()/embedded-device registration API in 3.10 (added 3.13), and 3.10 drivers pass their private state via `dev->dev_private` (exynos_drm_drv.c:63).

Required minimal header fix (no semantic change for callers):
    static inline struct exynos7580_device *to_exynos7580(struct drm_device *drm)
    {
    -	return container_of(drm, struct exynos7580_device, drm);
    +	return drm->dev_private;
    }
and main sets drm->dev_private = ex in ->load() (probe allocates ex via devm_kzalloc, kernel core owns the drm_device). The embedded `struct drm_device drm;` member then stays unused; keep it or drop it, your call.

Since the header is yours and frozen to me, I will write main.c against `drm->dev_private` semantics and use platform_get_drvdata(drm->platformdev) for the first access in ->load(). Say if you prefer allocating our own drm_device and calling drm_fill_in_dev() instead of drm_platform_init (that would keep container_of valid, but you explicitly asked for drm_platform_init).

