No O_NONBLOCK handling; fops use drm_open/drm_read directly.

Fix: add a wrapper read that forces O_NONBLOCK around drm_read:

```
static ssize_t exynos7580_read(struct file *filp, char __user *buf, size_t count, loff_t *ppos)
{
    unsigned int old = filp->f_flags;
    ssize_t ret;
    filp->f_flags |= O_NONBLOCK;
    ret = drm_read(filp, buf, count, ppos);
    filp->f_flags = old;
    return ret;
}
```
Race-y but for single reader acceptable.

