So O_NONBLOCK should work. But stack shows drm_read waiting → maybe our wrapper doesn't set it before drm_read due to... we set filp->f_flags |= O_NONBLOCK; but KWin may call read via io_uring/aio where filp differs? Or another thread reads a *different* fd opened by drm_open (we patch only the module's fops; all fds use it).

